Proposers are advised that proposal content and completeness are most important, and that clear
and effective presentations are preferred, with unnecessarily elaborate, decorative or extraneous
materials discouraged.  Each section within the proposal shall be clearly defined for easy reference.
 All blank spaces must be filled in (e.g., the number “0”, the word “None” or the words “Not
Applicable” or “NA” are to be inserted, where appropriate, on the forms).

B.
PROPOSAL FORMAT

The proposer shall use the following format.

Technical Proposal (Envelope #1)

1. Concession/Snack Shack Operations Team – The proposer should identify the operations
team members and their positions on the team and briefly outline the responsibilities and
experience of each member with in the proposed operation.

2. Concessions/Snack Shack Operations Area - The proposer should show briefly and
concisely their familiarity with the operations area.

3. Scope of Work - All proposers will commit at a minimum to the services outlined in “Exhibit
A – Scope of Work” and be prepared to enter into the proposed Professional Services
Agreement, draft copy attached.  The City and proposer may supplement the draft Scope of
Work with any additional work or clarification of work that is determined necessary for the
successful completion of the project.

4. References:   List at least three (3) references that would provide information regarding the
proposer’s qualifications to provide the referenced operation.  Use additional sheets if more
than three references are provided.  Provide the following information for each reference:
Name, Address, Relationship, Telephone # and an explanation of their knowledge of the
proposer’s ability to provide the referenced operation.

5. Project Specific Information - The proposer should carefully review “Exhibit A Scope of
Work,” “Exhibit B Allowable Operations,”  “Exhibit C Sample Schedule” and the attached
Professional Services Agreement. These exhibits provide background information and
directions necessary for proposal preparation.

6. Other Information - Any additional information the proposer feels would be useful to the
committee in evaluating the proposal should be placed in this section.

