### Page 22 of 38

```text
RFP-11-13
Pioneer Park Concession/Snack Shack Operations
Exhibit A

1

EXHIBIT A

SCOPE OF WORK

A. Project Description

The City of Cheyenne, Wyoming is seeking qualification statements and service proposals from
individuals or professionals experienced in the area of concessions/snack shack operations to address
the City of Cheyenne’s intent to provide concession/snack shack operations at the Pioneer Park
Baseball Field.  The specific nature of the scope of work for the project is outlined in this Request
for Proposals (RFP).  Proposers responding will be evaluated and a short list developed for formal
interviews to be conducted at a later date.  Such proposals shall be submitted to the City of
Cheyenne’s Purchasing Office, 2101 O’Neil Ave. Cheyenne, Wyoming by 2:00 p.m. February 21,
2013.

I.
Introduction and Background

The Pioneer Park Concession/Snack Shack is currently under construction.  The new facility will be
available for operations beginning April 1, 2013.  The facility will consist of the following:

 280 sq. ft. Concession Area
o Three (3) compartment industrial sink
o Ansul hood system
o Stainless steel counter top
o Serving window with an air curtain
o Hand washing sink
o Entry door.
 32 sq. ft. Storage Area
 Mechanical Room/Janitor’s Closet
o Floor sink.
 Family, Men’s & Women’s Restrooms
 Equipment, fixtures and furniture beyond the items listed are the sole responsibility of the
concession/snack shack provider.

The Pioneer Park Concession/Snack Shack is located at the Pioneer Park Baseball Facility.  This
baseball facility hosted approximately 160 games between April 1 and September 26, 2012.  The
majority of the games played occurred between in May (32), June (56) and July (42).  Typical users
of this facility include Senior Babe Ruth, American Legion Post 6, Cheyenne Mustang Baseball,
Adult Baseball and Cheyenne Grizzlies Baseball.

II.
Operation Objectives

The objectives of this RFP are:
```

### Page 23 of 38

```text
RFP-11-13
Pioneer Park Concession/Snack Shack Operations
Exhibit A

2


Secure a qualified concession/snack shack provider.

Provide a quality, consistent concessions/snack shack operation for baseball games
and tournaments scheduled at the Pioneer Park Baseball Field.

III.
Scope of Services

The minimum scope of services related to this operation includes the following:  [The Proposer is
invited to provide additional steps or work tasks as necessary or appropriate to assist in the
completion of the objective.]

A.
Menu & Pricing

 Provide a reasonably priced and varied menu for consumption by participants,
spectators and visitors to the Pioneer Park Center.
 Eliminate the sale of shelled items (i.e. sunflower seeds, peanuts) and chewing
gum.
 Beer sales are excluded.  All beer sales must be applied for and approved
through the City of Cheyenne Clerk’s Office, Police Department and the Parks
& Recreation Department.  The request for beer sales shall be made in writing
to the Parks & Recreation Department Administration Office.

B.
Consistent Opening/Closing

 Provide an operation that with a minimum of a 48 hour notice opens ½ hour prior
to each scheduled game/tournament.
 Provide an operation that provides services through the 2nd to last inning of the
last scheduled game each day.
 Provide an agreement where the contract can be voided in the event the stand is
not open for a certain number of games.

C.
Inspection Compliance & Permitting

 Provide an operation that complies with all applicable laws and regulations.
 Provide an operation that ensures all required City, County and State fees are paid
and current for concession operations.
 Provide an operation that complies with and passes all required inspections.

D.
Reduction of Waste

 Reduce the number of individually packaged/wrapped items (i.e. straw
wrapper, Jolly Rancher® candies).

E.
Other Items
```

